भव॑ m. coming into existence, birth, birthplace, origin
(often a. —˚ born of, sprung from, being in);
 becoming (—˚);
 being,
existence, world;
 means of existence, wealth, prosperity;
 N. of a god.

भाव m. becoming, being (often —˚);
 passing or change into
(loc. or —˚);
 occurrence, appearance, existence, duration;
 state,
condition;
 conduct, behaviour;
 nature, character, temper, disposition;
sentiment, feeling ((rh.));
 supposition, conjecture, meaning, sense;
 the
abstract idea of a verb (g.);
 affection, inclination;
 heart, soul, mind;
a being, thing, creature;
 a clever man, in respectful address =
honourable sir (d.).

भावन f. ई = भावक. — f. आ & n. effecting,
bringing about;
 imagination, conception, conjecture, supposition,
thought, idea;
 ascertainment, evidence (only f.).

भावनीय a. to be effected or accomplished;
 to be
fancied or imagined (n. impers.).

1 भ॑वन्त् (nom. भवन्) a. being, present;
 f. ˚न्ती the
present time or tense.

भाविक f. ई real, actual;
 sentimental, expressive;
 n.
lively expression.

भवित॑व्य a. = seq., n. impers. w. instr. of subj. &
pred.;
 abstr. ˚ता† f. necessity, fate, destiny.

भाविन् a. becoming, being (often —˚);
 what ought or is
about to be, impending, future. f. ˚नी a beautiful woman.

भविष्णु॑ a. being, becoming (only —˚);
 thriving,
prospering.

भाव्य॑ a. what ought to be, future (n. impers.);
 to be
caused or effected;
 to be (being) conceived or imagined, to be
convinced, to be demonstrated.

भावक a. causing, effecting, furthering, promoting (—˚
or gen.);
 fancying, imagining (gen. or —˚).

भावित a. brought into being, produced;
 enlivened,
refreshed, comforted, exalted;
 got, obtained;
 thought of, known;
 stated,
convicted;
 full of, occupied with (instr. or —˚), turned upon (loc.);
perfumed.

भा॑वुक a. becoming (w. nom. or —˚ after an adv. in
अम्);
